as of what we done give clarity below
===========================================


having 1 cluster and inside having 2 name spaces names called dev & test in dev have one pod, in test have one pod and have user also with name pranay
then for this user pranay need to give permissions for which present in inside the dev of pod only name space 
here we use role role-binding

vim role.yml

---
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: Role
metadata:
  name: dev-role
  namespace: dev
rules:
  - apiGroups: [""]
    resources: ["pods"]
    verbs: ["get", "watch", "list", "create"]

  - apiGroups: [""]
    resources: ["services"]
    verbs: ["get", "watch", "list"]

:wq



kubectl create -f role.yml --------------> command to execute above file

now we need to do role-binding

vim rolebinding.yml


---
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: RoleBinding
metadata:
  name: myrb1
  namespace: dev

subjects:
  - kind: User
    name: pranay
    apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io

roleRef:
  kind: Role
  name: dev-role
  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io


:wq


kubectl create -f rolebinding.yml -------------> commad to execute above manifest file

kubectl get rolebinding -n dev ---------------> command to view rolebinding 

kubectl config use-context devops -------------> command to switch user

as of now we gave permissions to a particular namespaces for that we used Role Role Binding

For now if we want to give permissions to all namespaces means we will use Cluster Role Cluster Role Binding like below

manifest files are similar and same to this also like below

cp role.yml cluster-role.yml

vim cluster-role.yml

---
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: ClusterRole
metadata:
  name: cluster-role
rules:
  - apiGroups: [""]
    resources: ["pods"]
    verbs: ["get", "watch", "list", "create"]

  - apiGroups: [""]
    resources: ["services"]
    verbs: ["get", "watch", "list"]

